WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.257
Here I have the example,

2
00:00:02.257 --> 00:00:04.230
"If I'm skilled at poker,

3
00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.387
then I'm gonna win a bunch of money."

4
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.760
So go to the casino,

5
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.820
I won a bunch of money playing poker

6
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.190
and I am tempted to conclude

7
00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.830
that therefore, I am skilled at poker.

8
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:20.220
Okay, so lots of people might actually believe this,

9
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.750
this would be a very reasonable

10
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.610
fallacy that a lot of people would make.

11
00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:27.180
Let's try to analyze it and I claim this is not true.

12
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:30.390
And the Liz idea is that just 'cause I won

13
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:32.070
a bunch of money, I might've just gotten lucky,

14
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:35.130
I might be terrible at poker, but I got really lucky.

15
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.290
So I cannot claim

16
00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:40.803
that I am skilled at poker from this argument.

17
00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.070
So let's try to analyze the structure of this argument.

18
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.980
First I have, if I'm skilled at poker,

19
00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.290
I'm gonna give that a P,

20
00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.923
then I will win money, I'm gonna give that as a Q.

21
00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.910
So that was my first premise, if P, then Q.

22
00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:01.910
So I'll write this as P implies Q, that is my first premise.

23
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:06.270
Next up I say, I won money playing poker.

24
00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:08.493
So this is asserting Q.

25
00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:13.260
And then what we're saying is P implies Q

26
00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.730
and I'm gonna copy it over here

27
00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:16.410
so that we have it all in place.

28
00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:18.660
P implies Q.

29
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.600
Then you assume the conclusion

30
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.213
and you're going to get, I'm skilled at poker.

31
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.820
So the logical form that you have here is P implies Q,

32
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.940
then Q, and then you get out P.

33
00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.370
But that wasn't modus pos, that wasn't modus tones,

34
00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.870
it was none of these.

35
00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:37.860
And the problem here

36
00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:40.762
is that you're kind of arguing by the converse.

37
00:01:40.762 --> 00:01:45.510
It's Q implies P would be the converse of the statement,

38
00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.710
not P implies Q.

39
00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.930
If you had Q implies P here,

40
00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.820
then you could icdate Q and get P,

41
00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.440
but not the other way around.

42
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.900
So this is trying to use

43
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.200
the converse of the statement and we know that a converse

44
00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.410
is not logically equivalent to the original statement.

45
00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:04.470
So this argument does not work.

46
00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:06.780
So this argument does not work

47
00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.990
and we are going to say that it is invalid,

48
00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:12.933
I disagree with this logical structure.

